documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:7:1. **Board selection.** Every A, B and test board is chosen to contain at least one safe and one unsafe non-king capture, all with complete certificates. The fly is told nothing about this, and it ranks **all legal moves**, but a safe answer always exists on the board. Uniform-random baselines (all legal, all captures, non-king captures) are reported beside every score to show how much this selection helps.
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:9:3. **Positive valence only.** A verified safe capture gets a +0.75 current into the 18 PAM07 cells. Unsafe captures get no external current. Unknown certificates produce no event.
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:10:4. **Success criterion.** Success is choosing a safe non-king capture. Quiet and king moves are legal choices that count as failures.
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:27:Neural, local APL unless named: **informative** (primary), **absent** (no external current), **off** (all persistent memory held fixed), **shuffled** (same pulse count, permuted within each phase), **informative-matched** (strength-matched nonlocal APL), **informative-global** (original scalar APL). Engineered comparisons, graph-free: **raw-pc** and **random-pc** nearest-episode stores (v5 transforms, capacity 4096, k 3) fed the same tape with the delivered pulse code, each also with the shuffled code. Uniform-random baselines.
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:33:T0 (naive), A8, A16, T_A (A end), T_B0 (after R1, before B), B8, B16, T_AB (B end), final (after R2). Test boards are ranked at T0, T_AB and final. Training boards are ranked at every checkpoint where revision 2 needs them. Every arm, the off arm included, ranks at every checkpoint, so pass counts are equal (changed after code review r1, before data; the earlier off-arm reuse of T0 rankings is withdrawn).
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:38:1. The only persistent state that changes is the ReversalMemory gain on the registered gamma-KC-to-MBON05 mask edges. Every other parameter, magnitude outside the mask, sign and topology keeps its T0 fingerprint at every checkpoint.
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:39:2. Every update is recomputed by the auditor from its receipt (actual KC rates, actual PAM07 rates, the Gkanias rule with eta 0.5, gain bounds 0.2-1.8, activity scale 1.5) and matches bit for bit.
documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-gates-2026-11-08.md:41:4. No engineered store, label, task ID or selected-action list enters the primary arm's scores (code review and auditor static check).
