 136: ## 16. 2026-11-08 23:41: dry run complete, "does not pass"; mechanism-level failure found
 137: 
 138: Dry run (development data, seed 7300; plumbing and cost check, not evidence): runner exit 0, manifest `complete`, verdict **does not pass**. Audit started 23:41 (pending).
 139: 
 140: - **Cost (measured):** 8,922 passes per job; local-APL arms 0.82 CPU-s and 1.33 s wall per pass with 6 workers (global arm 0.81 s wall); peak RSS 274-281 MiB; minimum free 2,778 MiB. All limits held.
 141: - **Gates:** P1.1 and P1.3 pass (mean D with pulse -0.468, without -0.0087). Every P2 and P3 gate fails: 0/8 A and 0/8 B boards acquired; test success 1/20 in informative = off = shuffled; 1,809/2,096 mask synapses changed >= 1% by T_AB, but no B-phase pressure write on A-written edges.
 142: - **Trace (mine, read-only, from records):** all legal moves on a board score within 5e-5 to 9e-5 of each other (MBON05 rate about 0.023). Learning shifts every move on a board by about +1.4e-4 together; the top move never changes. In every teaching replay all 2,096 gamma KCs are active (k about 0.011-0.015; rate mean 0.0165, sd 0.0015). KC patterns of two practised moves on one board differ by a median 2.6% (relative L2); of two boards, 3.5%.
 143: - **Hypothesis (not yet tested):** the model's gamma KC code is dense and nearly uniform, so the activity-gated source rule depresses almost all synapses equally and cannot separate moves on one board. If true, the registered full run (about 96 CPU-hours) would be a predictable P2/P3 failure.
 144: - **My mistake:** I built and dry-ran the pipeline without first checking the one quantity the rule needs, the move-specific part of the KC code. The handoff already recorded the warning (v2 pathway trace: the KC code shrinks the deciding one-piece difference 48 times). A short diagnostic of KC sparseness on the real graph before building would have shown this. The dry run caught it before the full run, so no confirmation data was spent.
 145: - **Next:** Codex mistake diagnosis (prompt `diagnosis-prompt-r1.txt`), then decide: run the full test as registered, redesign with a sourced fix (for example, KC sparseness calibrated to published active fractions), or stop for a researcher decision. No full run is launched until then.

