One protocol defect surfaced: the judge pools A and B when comparing learning with the absent, off, and shuffled controls. Its separate own-baseline checks reduce that risk, but a pooled positive result can still hide a control-comparison failure for one group. Revision 2 calls for A and B success to be assessed separately, so this needs a gate clarification before confirmation.
